<h2>Preventive Dental Care</h2>
<div class="divider"> </div>
<p>Preventing dental issues before they arise is the cornerstone of good dental care—but it becomes crucial when it comes to pediatric dentistry.</p>
<p>Children's teeth are growing, and thus more sensitive to issues such as gum disease or cavities. By protecting them early on and teaching your child the importance of building good oral hygiene habits, you can ensure their smile develops to the best of its condition.</p>
</div>
<div class="grid-3">
<div class="card"><span class="card-icon">🦷</span>
<h3>Dental Cleanings &amp; Exams</h3>
<p>Routine dental cleanings and exams are essential to maintaining your child's oral health. By scheduling visits every six months, we can catch potential problems early, prevent damaging decay, and suggest valuable treatments like orthodontics as soon as possible.</p>
