The issue is that the `<script>` tag is wrapped in `<p>` tags, which causes WordPress/CMS to mangle it. Here's the fixed accordion script — replace your current `<p><script>...</script></p>` block with this:

```html
<script>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
    document.querySelectorAll('.faq-q').forEach(function(btn) {
      btn.addEventListener('click', function() {
        var item = this.closest('.faq-item');
        var isOpen = item.classList.contains('open');
        document.querySelectorAll('.faq-item').forEach(function(i) {
          i.classList.remove('open');
          i.querySelector('.faq-q').setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
        });
        if (!isOpen) {
          item.classList.add('open');
          this.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
        }
      });
    });
  });
</script>
```

Two changes from your original:
1. **Removed the `<p>` wrapper** — WordPress wraps inline scripts in paragraph tags, which breaks execution
2. **Added `DOMContentLoaded`** — ensures the buttons exist before the script tries to attach listeners

If your CMS forces a `<p>` wrapper on any script tags, the safest alternative is to paste this into **Appearance > Theme Editor > footer.php** (before `</body>`) or use a plugin like "Insert Headers and Footers" to inject it cleanly.
